// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'dependent'. Valid alternatives: ['composite', 'shared', 'none']
//
// Property aggregation kind is a CLOSED set of three keywords. `(dependent)` is not a
// fourth kind the walker will reject later -- the parenthesised prefix is a token choice
// in the grammar, and the message enumerates the whole set.
//
// The parens make this dangerous. `(x)` in property-prefix position is also how a
// QUALIFIED property's parameter list begins, so a rewrite that reads "an identifier in
// parens" and maps it to an aggregation kind afterwards has a rule that accepts any word,
// and one that dispatches on the word first has to decide which construct it is looking at
// before it knows. legend-engine settles it in the lexer: only these three tokens can
// appear there at all.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::UnknownAggregation
{
   (dependent) owned: fixture::neg::Part[*];
}
